{
  "_what": "The one Calendar (src/calendar.mjs): every dated thing a person can see, read from every source here, in one list of items the Calendar screen (src/workspace/shared-calendar-screen.tsx) draws and the person's Focus narrows (src/record-scope.json lists). A source is read one of two ways: `route`, a GET to the person's own store with from and to (the same road their AI takes), or `tool`, one of their own Workshop tools run with `input` ({from} and {to} filled in), which is how a connected calendar is read through their own connection. `rows` is where its answer keeps the rows; `fields` says where each item field is read (a list of paths, the first one present wins); `ref` (a path, and an optional `prefix`) is the record a row is, so the Focus can keep it; `copies_of` drops a row that is the copy of another source's item put on a connected calendar (src/space-calendars.mjs keeps one record per meeting placed there, `record_type`:<item id>, whose `field` is the copy's id), so a meeting never shows twice. `look` is how its items read (label, icon, tone). `move` is the road that gives one of its items a new time when it may move (`post` and `body`, `{source_id}`, `{space_id}` and `{at}` filled in). `actions` are what an opened item offers, each a road: `post` with `body` (and `said` when done), `href` (an address to open), or `opens` (a screen of the workspace, by its id); `shows_when` shows it only while an item field `is` that value; `tone` `danger` marks one that takes something away, and `confirm` (`asks`, `yes`, `no`) has the person say yes before it runs. A source that cannot be read is said by its `unread` words and never stops the others. `connect` is where someone goes to connect a source that is not connected (straight to the service's own sign-in). A new source is one row here; `given` is every thing given to the person in their spaces that has a due date. `span_most_days` bounds one read; a source's `attendees`, `attendee_name` and `attendee_email` fields say where a provider keeps the people invited (at most MEETING_ATTENDEES_MOST, parts/record-audio/do-work/meeting-join-recording.ts, are kept on an item); `reuse_minutes` is how long a connected calendar's answer is used again before it is asked again, so moving between weeks does not ask Google each time.",
  "span_most_days": 62,
  "reuse_minutes": 10,
